 /** SoulGold v1.2.1: v1.2's struct but its attacks bit-packed ([PartyMonLayout.packedAttacks]). The game's own SetMonData
  * headless (moves 242 / 423 / 349 / 701, PP 15 / 15 / 20 / 10) wrote `f2 00 a7 01 5d e9 15 00 8f 07 45 31`; read as
  * v1.2's, move 4 came out 701 >> 5 = 21 and the PP 143 / 7 / 69 / 49 (a player's FISHIOUS REND read as SLAM). */
-val SOULGOLD_V1_2_1_PARTY_MON = SOULGOLD_PARTY_MON.copy(packedAttacks = true)
+val SOULGOLD_V1_2_1_PARTY_MON = SOULGOLD_PARTY_MON.copy(
+    packedAttacks = true,
+    // STATS (2026-11-21, a v1.2.1 save headless): EVs at +0x38 (the plaintext box's +0x18, as vanilla's), the IV word at +0x40
+    // (not vanilla's +0x48: five bits a stat, HP first), the nature the personality's. Each of a six-mon party's stats
+    // recomputes from these (base stats from gSpeciesInfo: 0x120-byte entries, HP / Atk / Def / Spe / SpA / SpD first), where the
+    // other offsets' did not. +0x12 is a nickname byte here, not a mint's nature: natureModifier off.
+    hasStats = true, plainIvWord = 0x20, natureModifier = false,
+)
 
